<title>SOUTH KOREA: SEOULBANK head under graft probe-report.</title>
<headline>SEOULBANK head under graft probe-report.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean prosecutors have questioned the president of SEOULBANK on allegations that he took bribes from several companies in return for help in getting loans approved, the state radio reported on Friday.</p>
<p>SEOULBANK's spokesman Koh Myoung-il denied the report.  </p>
<p>The Korean Broadcasting System quoted prosecution sources as saying SEOULBANK president Sohn Hong-gyun was alleged to have taken tens of millions of won from two to three companies.</p>
<p>Prosecution officials could not immediately be reached for comment.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
